{
  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "C1",
      "text": "The smallest building block in Java programs are functions.",
      "basis": "explicit",
      "availability": "SOURCE_SUPPORTED",
      "literal_kind": "verbal",
      "instructional_role": null,
      "refs": ["Q0001", "Q0002"],
      "related_refs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "C2",
      "text": "A function is a block of code that performs a task.",
      "basis": "explicit",
      "availability": "SOURCE_SUPPORTED",
      "literal_kind": "verbal",
      "instructional_role": null,
      "refs": ["Q0003", "Q0004"],
      "related_refs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "C3",
      "text": "Each button on a remote control performs a task, analogous to a function.",
      "basis": "explicit",
      "availability": "SOURCE_SUPPORTED",
      "literal_kind": "verbal",
      "instructional_role": null,
      "refs": ["Q0005", "Q0006", "Q0007"],
      "related_refs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "C4",
      "text": "Functions in programming languages are exactly the same.",
      "basis": "explicit",
      "availability": "SOURCE_SUPPORTED",
      "literal_kind": "verbal",
      "instructional_role": null,
      "refs": ["Q0009"],
      "related_refs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "C5",
      "text": "We can have functions for sending emails, converting weight, validating users, handling input, and so on.",
      "basis": "explicit",
      "availability": "SOURCE_SUPPORTED",
      "literal_kind": "verbal",
      "instructional_role": null,
      "refs": ["Q0010", "Q0011", "Q0012", "Q0013"],
      "related_refs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "C6",
      "text": "To code a function in Java, start by specifying the return type of that function.",
      "basis": "explicit",
      "availability": "SOURCE_SUPPORTED",
      "literal_kind": "verbal",
      "instructional_role": null,
      "refs": ["Q0014", "Q0015"],
      "related_refs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "C7",
      "text": "Some functions return a value like a number or a date, while other functions don't return anything.",
      "basis": "explicit",
      "availability": "SOURCE_SUPPORTED",
      "literal_kind": "verbal",
      "instructional_role": null,
      "refs": ["Q0016", "Q0017", "Q0018"],
      "related_refs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "C8",
      "text": "The return type of functions that don't return anything is void.",
      "basis": "explicit",
      "availability": "SOURCE_SUPPORTED",
      "literal_kind": "verbal",
      "instructional_role": null,
      "refs": ["Q0019", "Q0020"],
      "related_refs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "C9",
      "text": "After the return type, we have the name of the function.",
      "basis": "explicit",
      "availability": "SOURCE_SUPPORTED",
      "literal_kind": "verbal",
      "instructional_role": null,
      "refs": ["Q0021", "Q0022"],
      "related_refs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "C10",
      "text": "Give the function a proper descriptive name, like sendEmail, which clearly identifies its purpose.",
      "basis": "explicit",
      "availability": "SOURCE_SUPPORTED",
      "literal_kind": "verbal",
      "instructional_role": null,
      "refs": ["Q0023", "Q0024", "Q0025"],
      "related_refs": []
    }
  ],
